        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: rewrite published docs grounded in current source",
        "body": "Closes #100141\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where large parts of the published documentation (docs.openclaw.ai) were stale or inaccurate: pages written by an older model generation carried invented or outdated CLI flags, config keys, defaults, and behavior claims that no longer match the shipped code, wrapped in verbose filler that made pages hard to act on.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nFull source-grounded rewrite of the published docs corpus (529 files, every page reachable from `docs/docs.json` plus published non-nav pages). Each of 250 work units went through two independent passes:\n\n1. **Rewrite**: extract every load-bearing claim (commands, flags, config keys, defaults, env vars, paths, protocol/behavior statements), verify it against current `src/**`, `extensions/**`, `packages/**` and colocated tests, correct what is wrong, and rewrite the page dense and imperative under the `docs/AGENTS.md` Mintlify rules.\n2. **Adversarial verify**: diff old vs new for information loss (restore anything genuinely lost), re-verify the riskiest new claims against source, enforce mechanical rules (frontmatter, root-relative links, MDX validity, heading anchor safety).\n\nBoundaries: frontmatter `title:` values are byte-identical across all 529 changed pages (i18n glossary stability); generated surfaces (`docs/plugins/reference/**`, `plugin-inventory.md`, `docs_map.md`, `docs/maturity/**`) are regenerated, never hand-edited — now also documented in `docs/AGENTS.md`; internal working dirs (`docs/plan`, `docs/specs`, `docs/refactor`) untouched; curated release notes pages (`docs/releases/**`) left untouched by maintainer request. No file moves or renames; `docs.json` navigation unchanged. Branch history is incremental checkpoint commits; squash on merge.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers reading docs.openclaw.ai get accurate setup commands, real config keys with real defaults, and shorter pages that lead with what to do. The corpus shrank by ~9,300 net lines while gaining facts: 1,713 individual factual corrections were made against source, including real bugs (for example, the non-interactive onboarding example was missing the required `--accept-risk` flag and would have failed at runtime; the ACP migration doc named a config key that does not exist; several provider pages documented wrong catalog/default behavior).\n\n## Evidence\n\nScale and verification (per-unit JSON reports were produced by both passes):\n\n| Metric | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Files changed | 529 (`+31,633 / -40,848`, net `-9,215` lines) |\n| Rewrite units (rewrite + independent verify) | 250/250 completed |\n| Factual corrections vs source | 1,713 (753 with explicit `src/...:line` citations) |\n| Facts intentionally dropped as wrong/duplicate (logged per file) | 345 |\n| Claims kept but flagged unverifiable (logged per file) | 476 |\n| Facts restored by the verify pass | 143 |\n| Additional verify-pass fixes | 164 |\n\nGates, all green on this branch:\n\n- `node scripts/check-docs-mdx.mjs docs README.md` - passed (690 files)\n- `node scripts/docs-link-audit.mjs` - 5,698 internal links, 0 broken\n- `node scripts/check-docs-i18n-glossary.mjs` - passed (38 zh-CN glossary entries added for new short link labels; 0 title changes)\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check` - docs_map.md regenerated and in sync\n- `node scripts/generate-plugin-inventory-doc.mjs --check` - reference pages canonical (also fixes a pre-existing stale `codex.md`)\n- `scripts/docs-spellcheck.sh` - passed\n- Anchor validation: heading renames were tracked per unit; inbound anchors audited and fixed (6 links repointed). Mintlify's own `mint broken-links --check-anchors` could not run because of an upstream registry break (`@ark/util@0.56.1` unpublished, `mint@4.2.666` dep chain); a repo-local anchor audit (heading slugs + explicit `<a id>` tags) covers the gap. Rerun `pnpm docs:check-links:anchors` once upstream is fixed.\n\nSample corrections (each verified in source by both passes):\n\n- BlueBubbles migration: ACP binding key corrected to `match.channel` (`src/config/zod-schema.agents.ts`), config prose replaced with the real keys `attachmentRoots`, `mediaMaxMb`, `textChunkLimit`, and the missing SIP-disabled requirement for `imsg launch` added.\n- Onboarding automation: baseline non-interactive `openclaw onboard` example gained the unconditionally required `--accept-risk` (`src/commands/onboard.ts`).\n- NVIDIA provider: featured-catalog behavior now documents the 24h cache and 32-entry import as free text-input rows, and the fixed-host fetch policy.\n- Markdown formatting: per-channel spoiler and table-mode defaults now name the actual plugin defaults (`extensions/telegram/src/format.ts`, `extensions/signal/src/shared.ts`, `src/config/markdown-tables.ts`).\n- tlon channel: setup CLI example was missing the required `--url` flag; fixed by the verify pass.\n\nKnown limitations: 476 claims (mostly external-service behavior, e.g. third-party site UX) are kept and individually logged as unverified rather than silently trusted; residual per-unit review notes (310) are recorded in the run reports, none blocking.\n",
